I left one comment, on #944, and kept the issue open. The other seven issues got nothing: I didn't work on them this session and had nothing new to add.

#944 (commented, kept open). scripts/social.sh already turned on the audit record, took a per-run starting line count (a "watermark"), and had a separate "run never finished" state (no_terminal_emit, as opposed to zero). All three were added in an earlier session. The part that was broken was how it read the spend. It searched the agent's log for the ↳ usage line, but quiet mode never prints that line. So every social run that finished normally would have been reported as a run that died before writing its usage.

This session's two commits (20cbaff0, e5cf1d30) fix that. The script now reads the "type":"usage" records written after the watermark in the audit file. Four new cases in tests/harness_logic.sh cover:
• a finished run;
• two processes in one run;
• a run that really dies;
• a usage record from before the watermark not being counted.

To confirm the tests catch the old bug, I swapped the old search back in: 6 checks failed by name. After restoring it, 142 passed and 0 failed.

The comment also lists what's still missing:
• **Nowhere permanent to store it:** the spend only goes into the Actions log, which expires. There's no audit-log branch push like the one evolve.sh does.
• **Still no record:** scripts/dream.sh and the three yoyo --model calls in synthesize.yml still leave no usage record.
• **Totals are a lower bound:** sub-agent tokens still aren't counted (yologdev/yoagent#173).

